# Per-account DirectAdmin admin backups.
# Install: copy to /etc/cron.d/da-backup-batch (mode 644).
#
# DirectAdmin's own scheduled admin backup stages every account before the upload hook
# runs, which needs 66+ GiB of free space on a volume that has not had it since July 2026.
# It has been failing silently every night since. This entry replaces it with a run that
# archives one account at a time and lets the hook clear each one before the next starts.
#
# 01:00 leaves the whole run finished well before the oncallbrief pipeline at 03:45 and
# the weekly system backup at 05:00 on Saturdays -- none of the three should be competing
# for disk or for the backup lock. Cron mail is suppressed because the script's own
# alerting is the single notification path; a run that ends incomplete mails
# HEALTH_ALERT_TO with which accounts have no backup.
#
# Once this is running, delete DirectAdmin's own schedule at
# Admin Level -> Admin Backup/Transfer -> Schedule, or the two will race at 05:00.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin

0 1 * * * root /usr/local/sbin/da-backup-batch.sh >/dev/null 2>&1
